{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2","c3","c4"],"primary":"c2","title":"Santa Ana ban on algorithmic rent-setting software (Ordinance NS-3090)","requirement":"Prohibits the sale, licensing, provision and use of algorithmic rent-setting software (anticompetitive automated rent price-fixing) for residential rental property, including tools that set rents using nonpublic competitor data. Tenants may bring private claims for injunctive relief, damages or civil penalties, and the ordinance is also enforced through the city's code enforcement system.","key_value":"Civil penalties up to $1,000 per violation and per month","status":"in_force","effective_date":"2026-04-02","end_date":null,"citation":"Santa Ana Ordinance No. NS-3090","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental property within Santa Ana city limits.","exemptions":"Pricing software that relies solely on publicly available data or aggregate historical data, and tools used to comply with affordable housing program requirements (per D087).","conflict_note":"Status conflict: c4 (D087, published Feb. 24, 2026) records 'pending' because it reports only the Feb. 17 first reading and a final vote set for March 3, 2026. c3 (D086, March 9, 2026) reports that the final vote took place. c1 (D002) and c2 (D037) record the status as in_force with an effective date of 2026-04-02. The in_force status and 2026-04-02 effective date are kept because they are supported by later sources. All sources are secondary, so the date should be verified against the official ordinance. Penalty wording varies: c3 (D086) and c4 (D087) say $1,000 per violation, and c1 (D002) and c2 (D037) add 'per month'. These are treated as consistent."}],"dropped":[]}
